A share whose last ready thread waits stays on the run queue.
Its next turn would find no thread to run;
the run queue holds only shares with a ready thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: run queue holds a share it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -122,8 +122,6 @@ static void share_settle(struct share *s)
     bool owed = s->threads != 0 && s != turn;
     if (owed && s->next == NULL) {
         share_push(s);
-    } else if (!owed && s->next != NULL) {
-        share_remove(s);
     }
 }
 
